From: Armada <armada@armada.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] input: rsinput: accept large UART batches without dropping reports

The Duo journal repeatedly reports RX buffer overflow because serdev offers
more than 1024 bytes in one callback. The driver discards that entire batch
but returns count, telling serdev that every byte was consumed. It also
discards a partial frame when appending a smaller batch would overflow.

Accept only the remaining buffer capacity and return that accepted count.
The existing parser drains complete frames and retains the incomplete tail;
the tty receive loop retries the unconsumed bytes. This preserves frames
across buffer boundaries without enlarging the buffer or changing mappings.

--- a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
@@ -398,17 +398,8 @@
         return count;
     }
 
-    if (count > sizeof(drv->rx_buf)) {
-        dev_warn_ratelimited(&serdev->dev, "RX buffer overflow\n");
-        return count;
-    }
-
-    /*
-     * If the buffered partial frame plus the new bytes would overflow the
-     * buffer, discard the partial frame and resynchronise on the new bytes.
-     */
-    if (drv->rx_len + count > sizeof(drv->rx_buf))
-        drv->rx_len = 0;
+    /* Leave excess bytes with serdev to retry after this buffer is drained. */
+    count = min(count, sizeof(drv->rx_buf) - drv->rx_len);
 
     memcpy(drv->rx_buf + drv->rx_len, data, count);
     drv->rx_len += count;
